//! The runtime seams std defaults in a freestanding image: each a weak body a
//! runtime's own definition replaces, in the same compile or at the link
//! (runtime/ABI.md, "Weak defaults"). Only a freestanding compile loads this
//! module, and no program can import it. A hosted image's runtime defines
//! every seam strongly, so it gets none of these.

// A runtime with nothing to yield to has nothing to do here.
@weak
@export("__saw_rt_thread_yield")
func thread_yield() {
}
